-- The bus test (display-isolation, 2026-11-02): a Formula whose frame on
-- the VM is all IRAM-resident code — no draw stage, no table or helper
-- steps, only the lane loops the VM keeps in IRAM (`fast1`/`fast2`, the
-- grey colour) — so CPU0's traffic on the flash bus should not slow it.
-- Played with the JIT off (`display-stress.py --jit off`: the JIT's driver
-- runs from flash). If it holds steady under polls and uploads while
-- Starfield (a flash-resident draw stage) does not, the bus is confirmed.
name "IRAM light"
fps 100
v = frac(x*3 + y*2 + t)
gray(v)
